+// scroll, hover, the synthesised right click, and the key events at the bottom
+// - had its own copy of this, and they have to agree: a shortcut that is read
+// off a key event and a modified click that is read off a mouse event are the
+// same two keys to the person holding them down.
+//
+// Command is reported as m_controlDown because that is what wxOSX means by it:
+// CmdDown(), wxMOD_CONTROL and wxACCEL_CTRL all name the shortcut modifier,
+// which is Command on this family of ports, and every wx application is
+// written that way. The physical Control key is m_rawControlDown.
+//
+// AND SO IS CONTROL, WHEN COMMAND IS NOT HELD.
+//
+// An iPad takes any USB or Bluetooth keyboard and most of them are not
+// Apple's. On those, the key in the place the user reaches for a shortcut is
+// Control, and iPadOS reports it as Control because that is the key it is.
+// Reported honestly, every shortcut in the application above would be
+// reachable only from an Apple keyboard - which on a port whose whole premise
+// is a keyboard and a pointer is not a detail.
